{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q5005862","formula":"C₂₀H₂₆BrNOS","hill":"C20H26BrNOS","elements":["H","C","N","O","S","Br"],"composition":{"C":20.0,"H":26.0,"N":1.0,"O":1.0,"S":1.0,"Br":1.0},"names":{"en":"C-8813"},"descriptions":{"en":"C-8813 (thiobromadol) is a potent μ-opioid receptor agonist with a distinctive chemical structure which is not closely related to other established families of opioid drugs. The trans-isomer was found to be around 591 times more potent than morphine in animal studies. The same study assigned a potency of 504 times that of morphine to the related compound BDPC. C-8813 is claimed to be similarly potent at the δ-opioid receptor, which antagonizes the μ-induced depression of breathing, presumably making the drug safer."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":11058633,"mass":408.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN(C)C1(CCC(CC1)(CCC2=CC=CS2)O)C3=CC=C(C=C3)Br","inchikey":"XRDNIYBVNZLPJE-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"4-(4-bromophenyl)-4-(dimethylamino)-1-(2-thiophen-2-ylethyl)cyclohexan-1-ol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"11058633","atoms":50,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-3.973,"y":-4.563,"z":-0.289,"el":"Br"},{"x":4.993,"y":-1.472,"z":1.284,"el":"S"},{"x":1.416,"y":2.688,"z":-0.177,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.119,"y":2.153,"z":0.399,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.949,"y":1.3,"z":0.104,"el":"C"},{"x":1.058,"y":1.31,"z":-0.329,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.923,"y":1.505,"z":1.256,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.283,"y":1.86,"z":-1.187,"el":"C"},{"x":0.418,"y":0.815,"z":0.977,"el":"C"},{"x":0.072,"y":1.209,"z":-1.501,"el":"C"},{"x":2.337,"y":0.53,"z":-0.636,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.451,"y":-0.154,"z":0.005,"el":"C"},{"x":3.309,"y":0.584,"z":0.54,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.088,"y":2.083,"z":-0.694,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.739,"y":1.75,"z":1.659,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.879,"y":-0.656,"z":-1.22,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.473,"y":-0.955,"z":1.14